ther changing a protected secret can change an observable result in a way the stated policy forbids.</p><p class="example"><b>Example:</b> If public inputs stay the same, could public output distinguish two secret values that the policy says must remain indistinguishable?</p><p><b>Highest observed:</b> GPT-6 Sol (LLM, none) · 8/8 (100.0%)</p><details><summary>All 31 routes in this category</summary><div class="ranked-category"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Correct / questions (%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">GPT-6 Sol — no reasoning</th><td style="background:#081d58;color:#ffffff">8/8 (100.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Drex Max</th><td style="background:#243392;color:#ffffff">7/8 (87.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sonnet 5.5 — no thinking, JSON-choice</th><td style="background:#243392;color:#ffffff">7/8 (87.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Qwen3.8-Max — none, Hyper Charm</th><td style="background:#243392;color:#ffffff">7/8 (87.5%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fastino GLiDE</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mammoth-1</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Perplexity Decider v1.2</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Nimble v4 Max</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">d3-turbo</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Amos 1 Large</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">kettei-fat</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jev 1.14</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cloudflare Clef</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">6/8 (75.0%)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Microsoft-Decision-1</th><td style="background:#225da8;color:#ffffff">