</table></section><section id="image-support"><h2>Image results remain separate</h2><p>This Opus update is text-only; no Opus image score is inferred. <a href="https://etsabary.github.io/visual-decision-benchmark/report.html">Separate native-image benchmark</a>: Fastino 158/200, Amos 159/200. No image measurements changed.</p></section><section id="method"><h2>Method, costs and measurement limits</h2><p>31 full-bank routes: 27 specialized decision models and four selected no-reasoning LLM references. Each covers 1342 questions across 31 categories: 41,602 first attempts. Opus was measured October 23, 2026 (America/Toronto); all 30 earlier model records retain their original measurements and dates.</p><p>Opus used two requests per barrier wave, a 16-token output cap, explicit disabled thinking at high effort, no tools, the same frozen question/option order and numeric-only suffix, and an additional JSON-choice output grammar. The dated Anthropic standard endpoint was pinned with no provider fallback. All first attempts, including 37 refusals, stay in accuracy and latency denominators. No retries occurred. The mean, median and p95 pool all 1342 original response times, not category medians.</p><p>Opus API-reported cost totals $4.641065 for 1307 receipts; 35 refusal charges are unreported. Its separate successful synthetic probes total $0.002610; the disabled-thinking+xhigh negative control was rejected with HTTP400 and omitted cost telemetry. The separate eight-case bare-ID trial cost $0.019325 reported plus one unreported charge. These probes and the stopped trial are not pooled into the ranked bank. The positive high-effort probe returned zero thinking tokens; the negative control confirmed that xhigh is incompatible with disabled thinking on the tested route.</p><p>All 1305 usable Opus choices reported zero thinking tokens and no thinking blocks; 35 refusals omitted telemetry and are unverified, not verified zeros. Sonnet and Opus use separately labelled constrained JSON choice; Sol uses the bare-ID contract. These are selected references, not an exhaustive ranking of the strongest LLMs or a comparison with reasoning enabled.</p><p>Same frozen answer-free question bank, original options, native input and seed 2026101906. Every first attempt remains in the accuracy and latency denominator. One recovery is permitted only for transport failures or HTTP 408/429/5xx; Fastino additionally prespecified the documented HTTP 425 warming condition. No recovery was needed. No answer-dependent retries, batching of independent cases or provider fallback.</p><p>Fastino used two text requests per barrier wave and serial image requests. The text and image streams overlapped, with up to three Fastino calls globally. Timing starts before a fresh HTTPS connection and ends after the complete response body; encoding, queue, pacing and retry waits are excluded. The predeclared cumulative median cutoff is above 2000 ms after at least 20 questions. Provider hardware, load, dates and account limits remain confounds; these are observed route response times, not isolated inference throughput.</p><p>Fastino returned no monetary receipts. Its $0.04 per million input-token and $0 output tariff was captured from the authenticated catalog and documentation. Core text cost is $0.01739196; its separate text admission probe cost $0.00000364. Image core cost is $0.00767264 and two image probes cost $0.00010484. The combined usage-based cost including all probes was $0.02517308. Per-1000 values normalize actual bank totals; no extra 1000-question runs were made. Earlier missing charges remain unknown, not zero.</p><p>Native Fastino requests used store:false; all scored receipts reported not-stored retention. The response identity glide_v2 and catalog v2.2 description are recorded. Internal execution and immutable weights are not independently attested. LLM references retain their original protocol labels: Sol explicit reasoning off, Sonnet constrained JSON choice after a separate failed bare-ID trial, and Qwen none with missing reasoning-token telemetry not called zero.</p><p>This is a developing benchmark with uneven category sizes and dependent variants, not 1342 independent observations or a pristine held-out evaluation. The 37 permanent author-development exclusions retain their separate 1305-case diagnostic. Two audited ambiguous originals were replaced before these runs. The additions retain their verification evidence; the original bank received a targeted difficult-item audit rather than independent external verification of every original answer.</p><p>Answer keys, per-item correctness, raw account state and credentials stay outside public exports. Private frozen-key scoring, input reconstruction, full-ledger reconciliation, quantiles and exact-decimal cost sums were checked before publication. Public aggregate checks cannot independently reproduce answer correctness without the external reference key. Text and image banks remain separate.</p></section><section id="downloads"><h2>Questions, data and audit</h2><p><a href="opus5_reference_2026-10-23/statistics.json">31-route aggregate JSON</a> · <a href="opus5_reference_2026-10-23/model_statistics.csv">Model CSV</a> · <a href="opus5_reference_2026-10-23/category_scores.csv">Category CSV</a> · <a href="opus5_reference_2026-10-23/audit_receipt.json">Audit receipt</a> · <a href="opus5_reference_2026-10-23/manifest.json">Release manifest</a>.</p><p>Unchanged questions: <a href="consolidated_2026-10-19/questions_1342.csv">CSV</a> · <a href="consolidated_2026-10-19/questions_1342.jsonl">Native JSONL</a> · <a href="consolidated_2026-10-19/questions_1342.txt">Readable text</a>.</p></section></main></body></html>
